mapctx CLI

Commands:
  mapctx (no command)
    Opens the workspace UI (same as: mapctx workspace). Focuses the running UI if it is already up.
  mapctx workspace [path] [--add path] [--org id] [--org-name name] [--org-path path] [--target target-id] [--port n] [--no-open]
  mapctx workspace:add <path> [--org id] [--org-name name] [--org-path path]
  mapctx store init [--json]
    Materializes the local store. If plansAuthority=store but ~/.mapctx/projects/<id>/
    is missing entirely (lost machine, fresh clone, unrepairable corruption), this
    recovers from the last git-committed TASKS.md/tasks/*.md checkpoint into a fresh
    incarnation. Event history, claims, and cost/usage data strictly older than that
    checkpoint are permanently gone -- back up ~/.mapctx/projects/<id>/mapctx.db and
    commit checkpoints on your own cadence if you need more than that.
  mapctx store repair [--json]
  mapctx store attest-orphan <node-id> --reason "text" [--evidence key=value ...] [--json]
    Drafts a T-119 attestation pinning a DB-only node's complete event_log rows
    (journal-less, verifiable payload hashes only) and prints its content sha256.
    Writes nothing. Re-run with --approve-hash <sha256-from-the-draft> to write
    node-attestations.json, which lets `mapctx store repair` replay those rows and
    treat the node's absent prefix as a declared fact instead of a gap.
  mapctx import --dry-run [--json] [--tasks-file path]
  mapctx import --commit [--json] [--tasks-file path] [--config path] [--actor name]
  mapctx export [--reason manual|wave-end|epic-end] [--json]
  mapctx validate [--json] [--snapshots]
    Under store authority, default checks canonical store only. --snapshots explicitly checks local mirrors; failure returns non-zero.
  mapctx acceptance import [--commit] [--json]
    Dry-run by default; --commit imports observed checkboxes atomically, pins source bytes, skips existing revisions.
  mapctx task acceptance <show|revise|approve|unapprove> <task-id> [--from-file path] [--expect-revision n] [--criterion-id id|--index n] [--evidence key=value ...]
  mapctx task finish <task-id> [--json]
    Moves through canonical done gate, then publishes final checkpoint; retry after checkpoint failure is safe.
  mapctx task show <task-id> [--json]
  mapctx task context <task-id> --budget <n> [--json]
  mapctx task search --query "<text>" [--status <planning-state>] [--limit n] [--json]
    Duplicate-check helper: case/accent-insensitive AND match over title, tags, domains and
    summary from the task projection (title/tags/domains from TASKS.md pre-cutover). Title
    matches rank first; blank queries return no matches.
  mapctx plan [--json]
  mapctx gantt [--json]
  mapctx board [--json]
    Kanban board dataset (title/mode/tasks) for the workspace UI: TASKS.md
    pre-cutover, SQLite store under store authority (T-094).
  mapctx push [--dry-run] [--json] [--actor name]
    Store-backed GitHub projection (ADR 0003): reads canonical task projections from the SQLite
    store (never TASKS.md), checks store maintenance, remote conflicts and GitHub preconditions;
    local mirrors are not consulted (there is no snapshot-drift gate). Reconciles
    issues/status/dates in the GitHub repo+project bound in mapctx.toml [github].
    Requires the gh CLI authenticated.
  mapctx task claim <task-id> [--json] [--actor name] [--holder json]
  mapctx task start <task-id> [--dispatch-id id] [--executor kind] [--context-hash hash] [--status claimed|running] [--holder json] [--actor name] [--json]
    Atomically claims the task and creates a dispatch. Returns claimId, leaseToken, dispatchId and attempt; preferred execution entry point.
  mapctx task renew <task-id> --claim id --token token [--json] [--actor name]
  mapctx task release <task-id> --claim id --token token [--json] [--actor name]
  mapctx task create --title "<title>" [--id T-###] [--type epic|feature|task|bug|chore] [--parent id] [--status planning-state]
    [--priority p] [--workload w] [--tags a,b] [--domains d,e] [--depends-on a,b] [--blocking x,y]
    [--start date] [--due date] [--role r] [--impact i] [--effort e] [--summary s]
    `--effort` is agent active time: 1d=8 active hours, 1w=40 active hours. Executable tasks without workload or effort are warned and cannot be claimed.
    (--description text | --description-file path) [--json] [--actor name]
    Auto-assigns the next free id for the type prefix (E for epic, T otherwise). The
    description prose goes into the new detail file and stays Git-authored.
  mapctx task move <task-id> --status <planning-state> [--json] [--actor name]
    Legal transition under store authority (backlog|ready-for-do|doing|review|done|paused|cancelled|archived,
    or canonical backlog|ready|in-progress|review|done|paused|cancelled|archived). done stamps completedOn and
    releases any active claim; done also requires every current store Acceptance criterion to be approved.
    cancelled and archived release any active claim but do not stamp completedOn. cancelled means the
    work was aborted; archived means it will not proceed.
    Store-authority only: Markdown stays the editor pre-cutover.
  mapctx task reopen <task-id> --status review [--json] [--actor name]
    Reopens a done, cancelled, or archived task for review, clears completedOn, and records an audit event. Publish mirrors at an explicit checkpoint.
  mapctx task update <task-id> [--set key=value ...] [--depends-on a,b] [--blocking x,y] [--json] [--actor name]
    Whitelisted fields only (title,type,parentTaskId,priority,workload,tags,domains,startDate,dueDate,
    externalId,specMode,assignees,iteration,milestone; detail.* for role,impact,estimatedEffort,
    filesAffected,testsRequired,summary,prerequisites,blocking; waitReason=review|decision|parked|blocked-external).
    --depends-on/--blocking replace both
    the dependency edges and the detail prerequisites/blocking so the two surfaces never diverge.
  mapctx dispatch create <task-id> [--dispatch-id id] [--status claimed|running] (default claimed) [--executor kind] [--context-hash hash] [--json] [--actor name]
    New dispatch (fresh id, attempt 1) or --dispatch-id to append attempt max+1 to an existing one.
    Prints the dispatchId/attempt to feed `mapctx dispatch receipt`.
  mapctx dispatch receipt <dispatch-id> --receipt path [--claude-transcript path] [--other-session-activity path] [--idle-threshold-ms n] [--review-threshold-ms n] [--parked-threshold-ms n] [--time-zone zone] [--json]
  mapctx dispatch receipt <dispatch-id> --read --json
  mapctx reconcile <task-id> [--accept | --discard] [--json] [--actor name]
  mapctx sync status [--json]
  mapctx account add <name> [--currency USD] [--note text] [--json] [--actor name]
    Records a paid-plan account ("Codex Pro") in the store. Budgets and plan periods
    reference accounts; projects declare which accounts they draw from via `bind`.
  mapctx account list [--json]
  mapctx account bind <account-id-or-name> [--remove] [--json] [--actor name]
  mapctx plan-period record --account <id-or-name> --amount <decimal> --start <date|datetime>
    --end <date|datetime> [--currency c] [--plan-name n] [--seats n] [--json] [--actor name]
    Records the plan payment on the ACCOUNT (T-070: accounts own plans, projects consume).
  mapctx budget set <epic-id> (--amount <decimal> | --minutes n) [--currency USD] [--start date]
    [--end date] [--note text] [--json] [--actor name]   (--project targets the whole project)
    Event-sourced: every set is a revision; history is kept, latest wins.
  mapctx budget status <epic-id> [--json]   (--project for the whole project)
    Planned/spent/remaining/spent% from the cost chain. Scopes with no cost data say
    "no cost data" -- never zeros that look measured.
  mapctx budget history <epic-id> [--json]
  mapctx history scan [--dry-run | --commit --approve <file>] [--emit-approval-template <path>] [--include-inferred] [--json] [--codex-sessions dir] [--opencode-db path] [--claude-dir dir] [--repo dir] [--task T-1,T-2]
    --emit-approval-template writes approval CANDIDATES (schemaVersion 2, source-hash pinned)
    from the dry-run. Degraded mixed-provenance sessions are EXCLUDED unless --include-inferred
    opts them in as explicit intendedTier "inferred" candidates. It is not an approval:
    prune, review, then pass to --commit --approve.
    Links local Codex/OpenCode/Claude sessions plus git to tasks by signal
    strength (T-101), scoped to this repository/worktree identity (T-116):
    sessions from other repositories and sessions with unverifiable cwd are
    listed but never linked. --dry-run reports tiers/intervals/confidence and
    writes nothing; --commit records approved links as historical evidence
    through the journal -- no claim/dispatch/receipt, no lifecycle mutation,
    works for done tasks too -- and refreshes the measured-date cache.
  mapctx history correct <task-id> --target receipt:<dispatchId>/<attempt> | evidence:<id> --because "<reason>" [--json]
    Journals an auditable correction: the original receipt/evidence stays
    queryable, but invalid evidence drops out of roadmap + calibration.
    Receipt targets must be exactly <canonical-uuid>/<positive-attempt>.
  mapctx history reconstruct [--json] [--task T-1,T-2]
    Rebuilds the approved history view after corrections, tiering tasks
    measured / inferred / declared / synthetic / no-history.
